1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,830
“By 35, you'll see who took risks and who didn't.”

2
00:00:02,850 --> 00:00:04,486
That's Tim Denning,

3
00:00:04,506 --> 00:00:07,260
whose bio claims 1B+ views and $6M+ earned.

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:09,482
An Aussie who says he spent ten years in banking,

5
00:00:09,502 --> 00:00:12,360
then quit in 2021 to write online.

6
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:14,515
First published in 2025, written at 38:

7
00:00:14,535 --> 00:00:17,600
these 36 lessons have drawn 28 million views on X.

8
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:19,353
Lesson 1: how old you feel depends

9
00:00:19,373 --> 00:00:20,410
on how you lived.

10
00:00:20,430 --> 00:00:22,225
Playing it safe stacks up regrets,

11
00:00:22,245 --> 00:00:23,890
and regrets age you faster.

12
00:00:23,910 --> 00:00:25,245
Decisions keep getting pushed to later,

13
00:00:25,265 --> 00:00:26,780
when nobody is accountable.

14
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:28,608
Overthinking a $100 purchase?

15
00:00:28,628 --> 00:00:30,480
Tim's reply: wake up.

16
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:32,900
Lesson 4: raise your standards until people call you crazy.

17
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:34,290
Never settle for average.

18
00:00:34,310 --> 00:00:35,669
Tim says people who call you crazy

19
00:00:35,689 --> 00:00:37,100
are just making excuses for themselves.

20
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:39,388
Higher standards make decisions for you:

21
00:00:39,408 --> 00:00:41,900
less binge-watching, less drinking, less sitting.

22
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:43,664
Lesson 5: skip the conventional path.

23
00:00:43,684 --> 00:00:45,960
It's the most boring and the most crowded.

24
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:47,480
The standard path, per Tim:

25
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:48,858
a degree, some debt,

26
00:00:48,878 --> 00:00:51,030
and a job you pretend is your life's work.

27
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:52,794
How did Tim notice? Always bored,

28
00:00:52,814 --> 00:00:55,220
and the whole week was predictable.

29
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:56,212
The only suspense:

30
00:00:56,232 --> 00:00:58,910
a beef burger or a chicken burger for lunch.

31
00:00:58,930 --> 00:01:00,569
Lesson 6: hearing an opinion you disagree

32
00:01:00,589 --> 00:01:02,740
with without getting emotional is a sign of intelligence.

33
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:04,031
Labels make us dumber.

34
00:01:04,051 --> 00:01:06,680
The world is too nuanced for 'this or that'.

35
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:09,352
But it's all personal experience, with no study cited.

36
00:01:09,372 --> 00:01:12,090
Tim admits he's 'not that smart'.

37
00:01:12,110 --> 00:01:14,344
Regret piles up one 'later' at a time.

38
00:01:14,364 --> 00:01:16,920
Thirty-five just comes to collect.
